---
title: Tuning and feedback loop — how a firing rule changes
---
flowchart LR
  RUN["Rule runs on schedule<br/>queryFrequency · queryPeriod"] --> ALERT["Alert raised<br/>entity-mapped"]
  ALERT --> INC["Incident<br/>grouped by entity"]
  INC --> TRIAGE["Triage<br/>disposition per the SOP"]
  TRIAGE --> CLASS{"Classification"}
  CLASS -->|"true positive"| IR["Incident response<br/>contain · eradicate · recover"]
  CLASS -->|"false positive"| TLOG["Tuning log entry<br/>benign pattern · proposed change · owner · due date"]
  CLASS -->|"benign positive"| TLOG

  TLOG --> DECIDE{"What kind of change?"}
  DECIDE -->|"threshold"| TH["Edit the named let binding<br/>rule metadata.tuningGuidance updated"]
  DECIDE -->|"known-good actor"| WL["Watchlist exclusion<br/>owned and reviewed, not a query edit"]
  DECIDE -->|"gap in the rule"| Q["Rewrite the query"]
  DECIDE -->|"acceptable noise"| ACC["Accepted risk<br/>recorded with a named owner"]

  TH --> VER["Version bumped · CI must pass"]
  Q --> VER
  WL --> VER
  VER --> LEDGER["Validation ledger checked:<br/>did the evidence path change?"]
  LEDGER --> RUN

  IR --> METRICS["Metrics recorded<br/>volume · precision · latency · MTTA · MTTR"]
  ACC --> METRICS
  METRICS --> RUN

  NOTE["Measured values live in tests/validation/performance-metrics.md.<br/>The per-rule framework is generated: docs/metrics-matrix.md"] --- METRICS
